{"t": 1794118847.9263024, "kind": "call", "tool": "atlassian_jira_add_comment", "args": {"issue_key": "PAY-618", "body": "Implemented the agreed fix in `checkout.promo.normalize_code` (repo working tree `checkout/promo.py`).\n\nThe function now normalises codes before lookup:\n- strips surrounding whitespace\n- removes inner whitespace\n- upper-cases the result\n\nImplementation: `return \"\".join(code.split()).upper()`\n\nVerified locally: `\" autumn24 \"`, `\"au tumn 24\"`, `\"\\tAutumn 24\\n\"`, and NBSP-padded variants all normalise to `AUTUMN24`; an already-clean `AUTUMN24` is unchanged. This addresses the Android keyboard behaviour seen in Sentry issue CHECKOUT-WEB-7Q (code `' autumn24 '`)."}, "ok": true}
